==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ən/|a=weak form}}, {{enPR|ən}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Pvanp7-in a while (unstressed).wav|text=in a while|a=UK,weak form|IPA=/ən‿ə waːl/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪn/|a=strong form}}, {{enPR|ĭn}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-in.ogg|a=US,strong form}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Pvanp7-in (stressed).wav|a=UK,strong form}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-in.ogg|a=AU,strong form}}
* {{IPA|en|/ən/|a=NZ,strong form}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪn|s=1}}<!--No ən rhyme: can't rhyme a weak form word.-->
* {{homophones|en|an|qq1=weak form|and|qq2=weak form|inn}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=preposition|:inh|enm:in<id:preposition>}}
{{PIE word|en|h₁en}}
Preposition and verb from {{inh|en|enm|in}}, from {{inh|en|ang|in}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*in}}.{{dercat|en|ine-pro|inh=1}}

Adverb, noun and adjective from {{inh|en|enm|in}}, from {{inh|en|ang|inn}} and {{m|ang|inne}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*innai}}.

Sense 1/2 "in"/"into" are from the original PIE prefix, with locative/accusative case respectively. Sense 3/4 "qualification"/"means" are from the PIE metaphor of all infinitives coming from locatives.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|i'||colloquial|poetic}}

====Preposition====
[[File:Le Bounty.jpg|thumb|right|A ship '''in''' a bottle.]]
[[File:Bichon Frisé in sink.jpg|thumb|right|A dog '''in''' a sink.]]
{{en-head|prep}}

# {{non-gloss|Used to indicate location, inclusion, or position within spatial, temporal or abstract limits.}}
## [[contain|Contained]] by; [[inside]].
##: {{ux|en|The dog is '''in''' the kennel.}}
##: {{ux|en|There were three pickles '''in''' a jar.}}
## [[within|Within]] the bounds or limits of.
##: {{ux|en|I like living '''in''' the city.}}
##: {{ux|en|There are lots of trees '''in''' the park.}}
##: {{ux|en|He sat '''in''' the chair.}}
##: {{ux|en|She stood '''in''' the spotlight.}}
##* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-08-03|volume=408|issue=8847| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21582498-america-has-changed-way-it-measures-gdp-boundary-problems Boundary problems]| passage=GDP measures the total value of output '''in''' an economic territory.}}
## [[surround|Surrounded]] by; [[among]]; [[amidst]].
##: {{ux|en|We are '''in''' the enemy camp.}}
##: {{ux|en|Her plane is '''in''' the air.}}
##: {{ux|en|Waiter! There's a fly '''in''' my soup!}}
## {{senseid|en|wearing}} Wearing (an item of clothing).
##: ''I glanced over at the pretty girl '''in''' the red dress.''
##: ''Who’s the blonde '''in''' the sunhat over there?''
## {{n-g|Expressing abstract containment.}}
##: {{ux|en|There wasn't much of interest '''in''' her speech.}}
##: {{ux|en|He hasn't got an original idea '''in''' him.}}
## [[part|Part]] of; a [[member]] of; out of; from among.
##: {{ux|en|You are one '''in''' a million.}}
##: {{ux|en|She's '''in''' an orchestra.}}
## {{senseid|en|during}} [[during|During]] (a period of time or event).
##: {{ux|en|My birthday is '''in''' the first week of December.}}
##: {{ux|en|Easter falls '''in''' the fourth lunar month.}}
##: {{ux|en|The country reached a high level of prosperity '''in''' his first term.}}
##: {{ux|en|We lost that painting '''in''' the move to our new house.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:National Geographic|year=1989|month=May|volume=175|number=5|title=Venezuela's Islands in Time|author=Uwe George|page=542
|text=Dr. Brewer-Carias, who discovered the canyon '''in''' 1976, named is Valle de los Cristales—"valley of the crystals."}}
## {{senseid|en|within}} [[within|Within]] (a certain elapsed time); by the end of.
##: {{ux|en|Will you be able to finish this '''in''' a week?}}
##: {{ux|en|The massacre resulted in over 1000 deaths '''in''' three hours.}}
## {{senseid|en|at the end}} At the end of (a period of [[time]]).
##: {{ux|en|They said they would call us '''in''' a week.}}
## Participating in a field, activity or industry.
##: {{ux|en|I've always worked '''in''' plastics.}}
##: {{ux|en|She dabbles '''in''' Buddhism.}}
## {{lb|en|grammar|phonetics}} Characterized by.
##: {{ux|en|Many English nouns '''in''' ''-is'' form their plurals '''in''' ''-es'', while those '''in''' ''kn-'' are pronounced just /n/-.}}
# As to enter; from outside to inside; [[into]].
#: {{ux|en|Less water gets '''in''' your boots this way.}}
#: {{ux|en|She stood there looking '''in''' the window longingly.}}
## As to enter a [[driveway]], [[parking lot]], etc.
##: {{ux|en|Turn '''in''' to the second house on the left.}}
# [[by|By]] (doing something); {{n-g|indicating action causing an effect or achieving a purpose}}.
#: {{ux|en|'''In''' replacing the faucet washers, he felt he was making his contribution to the environment.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''In''' trying to [[make amends]], she actually [[made matters worse]].}}
#: {{ux|en|My aim '''in''' travelling there was to find my missing friend.}}
#: {{ux|en|Although severely provoked, she showed admirable restraint '''in''' not retaliating.}}
#* {{RQ:Falkner Moonfleet|year=1934|passage='''In''' returning to the vault, I had no very sure purpose in mind; only a vague surmise that this finding of Blackbeard's coffin would somehow lead to the finding of his treasure.}}
# {{non-gloss|Indicating an order or arrangement.}}
#: {{ux|en|My fat rolls around '''in''' folds.}}
#: {{ux|en|The planes flew over '''in''' waves.}}
#: {{ux|en|Arrange the chairs '''in''' a circle.}}
# {{senseid|en|state}} {{non-gloss|Denoting a [[state]] of the subject.}}
#: {{ux|en|He stalked away '''in''' anger.}}
#: {{ux|en|John is '''in''' a coma.}}
#: {{ux|en|My fruit trees are '''in''' bud.}}
#: {{ux|en|The company is '''in''' profit.}}
# {{non-gloss|Indicates, connotatively, a place-like form of someone's (or something's) personality, as his, her or its psychic and physical characteristics.}}
#: {{ux|en|You've got a friend '''in''' me.}}
#: {{ux|en|He's met his match '''in''' her.}}
# {{senseid|en|pertaining}} [[pertaining|Pertaining]] to; [[with regard to]].
#: {{ux|en|There has been no change '''in''' his condition.}}
#: {{ux|en|What grade did he get '''in''' English?}}
#: {{co|en|six inches '''in''' depth}}
# As to have [[sufficient]] or [[plentiful]] amounts of.
#: {{ux|en|The fruit trees in the yard keep me '''in''' apples and pears for most of the year.}}
# {{non-gloss|Used to indicate means, medium, format, genre, or instrumentality.}}
## {{lb|en|of something offered or given in an exchange}} In the form of, in the denomination of.
##: {{ux|en|Please pay me '''in''' cash — preferably '''in''' tens and twenties.}}
##: {{ux|en|The deposit can be '''in''' any legal tender, even '''in''' gold.}}
##: ''Her generosity was rewarded '''in''' the success of its recipients.''
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Carla Bethmann|title=Clean, Friendly, Profitable?: Tourism|page=114
|passage={{...}} tourists sometimes attempt to pay '''in''' euros or British pounds.}}
## {{non-gloss|Used to indicate a language, script, tone, etc. of a text, speech, etc.}}
##: {{ux|en|Beethoven's "Symphony No. 5" '''in''' C minor is among his most popular.}}
##: {{ux|en|His speech was '''in''' French, but was simultaneously translated into eight languages.}}
##: {{ux|en|When you write '''in''' cursive, it's illegible.}}
##: {{ux|en|Military letters should be formal '''in''' tone, but not stilted.}}

