=====Translations=====
{{see translation subpage|Preposition}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To [[enclose]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To take in; to [[harvest]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare All's Well|I|iii|passage=He that ears my land spares my team and gives me leave to '''in''' the crop.}}

====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# At or towards the [[interior]] of a defined space, such as a building or room.
#: {{ux|en|Suddenly a strange man walked '''in'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Would you like that to take away or eat '''in'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|He ran to the edge of the swimming pool and dived '''in'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=II|passage=Orion hit a rabbit once; but though sore wounded it got to the bury, and, struggling '''in''', the arrow caught the side of the hole and was drawn out. Indeed, a nail filed sharp is not of much avail as an arrowhead; you must have it barbed, and that was a little beyond our skill.}}
# Towards the speaker or other reference point.
#: {{ux|en|They flew '''in''' from London last night.}}
#: {{ux|en|For six hours the tide flows '''in''', then for another six hours it flows out.}}
# So as to be enclosed or surrounded by something.
#: {{ux|en|Bring the water to the boil and drop the vegetables '''in'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was tired enough to snuggle '''in''' with the dogs on the couch and sleep there.}}
# After the beginning of something.
#: {{ux|en|The show still didn't become interesting 20 minutes '''in'''.}}
# {{lb|en|in combination, after a verb}} {{n-g|Denotes a gathering of people assembled for the stated activity, sometimes, though not always, suggesting a protest.}}
#: ''sing-'''in''''', ''pray-'''in''''', ''hug-'''in'''''; ''see also [[be-in]], [[love-in]], [[sit-in]], [[teach-in]].''

=====Translations=====
{{see translation subpage|Adverb}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[position]] of [[power]] or [[influence]], or a way to get it.
#: {{ux|en|His parents got him an '''in''' with the company.}}
# {{lb|en|mostly|in the plural}} One who, or that which, is in; especially, one who is in office.
#: {{antonyms|en|out}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1827|author=Benjamin Chew|title=A Sketch of the Politics, Relations, and Statistics, of the Western World|page=192
|passage=This memoir has nothing to do with the question between the '''''ins''''' and the ''outs''; it is intended neither to support nor to assail the administration; it is general in its views upon a general and national subject; {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|sport}} The state of a [[batter]]/[[batsman]] who is [[currently]] [[batting]]; see {{m|en|innings}}.

