====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|not comparable}} Located [[indoors]], especially at home or at one's office or place of work.
#: {{ux|en|Is Mr. Smith '''in'''?}}
# {{lb|en|not comparable}} Located [[inside]] something.
#: {{ux|en|Little by little I pushed the snake into the basket, until finally all of it was '''in'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The bullet is about five centimetres '''in'''.}}
# {{lb|en|sports|of the ball or other playing implement}} Falling or remaining within the bounds of the playing area.
#: {{ux|en|If the tennis ball bounces on the line then it's '''in'''.}}
# Inserted or fitted into something.
#: {{ux|en|I've discovered why the TV wasn't working – the plug wasn't '''in'''!}}
# Having been collected or received.
#: {{ux|en|The replies to the questionnaires are now all '''in'''.}}
## [[in stock|In stock]], [[available]] in stores (particularly of a [[new]] item).
##: {{ux|en|Our latest product is '''in'''!}}
# In fashion; popular.
#: {{ux|en|Skirts are '''in''' this year.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1996|artist={{w|Pantera|Pantera}}|title={{w|The Great Southern Trendkill|The Great Southern Trendkill}}|passage=Pierce a new hole<br/>If Hell was '''in''' you'd give your soul<br/>To the great southern trendkill}}
# Incoming.
#: {{ux|en|the '''in''' train}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|of the sails of a vessel}} Furled or stowed.
# Of the tide, at or near its highest level.
#: {{ux|en|You can't get round the headland when the tide's '''in'''.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} With privilege or possession; used to denote a holding, possession, or [[seisin]].<ref>{{R:Burrill Law Dictionary}}</ref>
#: {{ux|en|'''in''' by descent;&emsp;'''in''' by purchase;&emsp;'''in''' of the seisin of her husband}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} Currently batting.
# Having [[familiarity]] or [[involvement]] ''with'' somebody.
#: {{ux|en|He is very '''in''' with the Joneses.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Joe R. Lansdale|title=Flaming Zeppelins: The Adventures of Ned the Seal|page=123|passage=“{{...}} He {{...}} took a rifle out of the batch and shot at me. I was lucky he was such a crummy shot.”<br>“Why would he do that?”<br>“I think he's '''in''' with them, Doctor.”<br>“Them? You mean Ned and Cody?”<br>“All of them. Hickok, the split tail, the whole lot.”}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} Having a favourable position, such as a position of influence or expected gain, in relation to another person.
#: {{ux|en|I need to keep '''in''' with the neighbours in case I ever need a favour from them.}}
#: {{ux|en|I think that bird fancies you. You're '''in''' there, mate!}}
# {{lb|en|of fire or fuel}} {{lb|en|Britain|Ireland|Australia|New Zealand}} Burning; ablaze.
#* {{quote-book|en
|year=1888
|author=H.C. O’Neill; Edith A. Barnett
|title=Our Nurses and the Work They Have to Do
|url= https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Our_Nurses_and_the_Work_They_Have_to_Do/nEJn0jog6msC?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=“Keep+the+fire+in”&dq=“Keep+the+fire+in”&printsec=frontcover
|page=81
|passage=Blocks of compressed coal keep the fire '''in''' for a long time, but they give out very little heat.}}
#* {{quote-book|en
|year=1894
|author=Henry Kingsley
|title=The Recollections of Geoffry Hamlyn - Volume 2
|url=https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/The_Recollections_of_Geoffry_Hamlyn/jXU-AAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=“the+fire%27s+in”&pg=PA183&printsec=frontcover
|page=183
|passage=“At all events,” said the Doctor, “the fire’s '''in''', and here’s the camp-oven, too. Somebody will be here soon. I will go in and light my pipe.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en
|year=1901
|author=William Francis Barry
|title=The Wizard’s Knot
|url=https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/The_Wizard_s_Knot/AaYlAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=“keep+the+fire+in+while”&dq=“keep+the+fire+in+while”&printsec=frontcover
|page=231
|passage=Was there any person in your own house at Renmore to keep the fire '''in''' while you were here?.}}
#* {{quote-book|en
|year=2011
|author=Rosemary Sutcliff
|title=The Eagle of the Ninth Chronicles
|url= https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/The_Eagle_of_The_Ninth/BaruAwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=“keep+the+fire+in+while”&pg=PT118&printsec=frontcover
|page=
|passage=Normally when they camped in the wild they took turns to sit up and keep the fire '''in''' while the others slept, […].}}
#* {{quote-book|en
|year=2019
|author=A.L.Lester
|title=Shadows on the Border
|url= https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Shadows_on_the_Border/-HmIDwAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=“Keep+the+fire+in+overnight”&pg=PT184&printsec=frontcover
|page=
|passage=He turned and started making up the range to keep the fire '''in''' overnight, and heard the front door click and Grant’s motor fire up. Sleep. He needed to sleep.}}
# Having [[use]]d, [[consume]]d {{,}} or [[investe]]d a certain amount.
#: {{ux|en|I'm three drinks '''in''' right now.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was 500 dollars '''in''' when the stock crashed.}}

